SetCreationTimestampIntegrationConcreteTest
├── When the caller is not the owner
│   └── It should revert with {OwnableUnauthorizedAccount}
└── When the caller is the owner
    ├── When the pool is the zero address
    │   └── It should revert with {ZeroAddress}
    └── When the pool is not the zero address
        ├── When the creation timestamp is zero
        │   └── It should revert with {ZeroTimestamp}
        └── When the creation timestamp is not zero
            ├── When the creation timestamp is equal or greater than the block timestamp
            │   └── It should revert with {InvalidTimestamp}
            └── When the creation timestamp is smaller than the block timestamp
                ├── When the pool is not registered in pool launcher 
                │   └── It should revert with {PoolNotInPoolLauncher}
                └── When the pool is registered in pool launcher
                    ├── It should set a new timestamp for the pool
                    └── It should emit a {CreationTimestampSet} event
